      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the  minimum value of z = x^2 +2y^2+6x+2, we can complete the square.\n\nx^2 + 6x + 2y^2 + (18y) + 2 + (16y)^2 - 22 = 0\n\n(x + 3)^2 + (18y)^2 - 22 = 0\n\n(x + 3)^2 + 18y^2 = 22\n\nWe let x+y=z\n\n(x + 3)^2 + 18((z-x)/2)^2 = 22\n\n(x+3)^2+9x^2+(z-x)^2 = 22\n\n10x^2+2xz+x^2+6x+4y^2-22 = 0\n\n10x^2+2xz+z^2+(z-3/2)^2 = 26\n\nThe minimum value occurs when (z-3/2)^2 >= 0\n\nSo, z = (26-(z-3/2)^2)/10\n\nIf (z-3/2)^2 > 0, we have\n\nz = (26-(z-3/2)^2)/10.\n\nIf (z-3/2)^2 = 0, we have\n\nz = twice the value found with the first solution.",
